# Date Functions Practice

## Q1. Display the current date.

```sql
SELECT CURDATE() AS current_date;
```

## Q2. Display the current date and time.

```sql
SELECT NOW() AS current_datetime;
```

## Q3. Extract the joining year of each employee.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       YEAR(joining_date) AS joining_year
FROM employees;
```

## Q4. Extract the joining month of each employee.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       MONTH(joining_date) AS joining_month
FROM employees;
```

## Q5. Extract the joining day of each employee.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DAY(joining_date) AS joining_day
FROM employees;
```

## Q6. Display the weekday name of the joining date.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DAYNAME(joining_date) AS joining_day_name
FROM employees;
```

## Q7. Display the month name of the joining date.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       MONTHNAME(joining_date) AS joining_month_name
FROM employees;
```

