# Date Calculation Functions

## Q8. Find how many days each employee has been working in the company.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DATEDIFF(CURDATE(), joining_date) AS days_in_company
FROM employees;
```

## Q9. Find the date 30 days after the joining date.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DATE_ADD(joining_date, INTERVAL 30 DAY) AS after_30_days
FROM employees;
```

## Q10. Find the date 1 year after the joining date.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DATE_ADD(joining_date, INTERVAL 1 YEAR) AS after_1_year
FROM employees;
```

## Q11. Find the date 6 months before the joining date.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DATE_SUB(joining_date, INTERVAL 6 MONTH) AS before_6_months
FROM employees;
```

## Q12. Calculate the current age of each employee.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, birth_date,
       TIMESTAMPDIFF(YEAR, birth_date, CURDATE()) AS age
FROM employees;
```

