# Challenge Practice

## Q23. Find employees who have more than 3 years of experience.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       TIMESTAMPDIFF(YEAR, joining_date, CURDATE()) AS experience
FROM employees
WHERE TIMESTAMPDIFF(YEAR, joining_date, CURDATE()) > 3;
```

## Q24. Find employees whose age is greater than 25.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, birth_date,
       TIMESTAMPDIFF(YEAR, birth_date, CURDATE()) AS age
FROM employees
WHERE TIMESTAMPDIFF(YEAR, birth_date, CURDATE()) > 25;
```

## Q25. Find IT employees who joined in 2022.

```sql
SELECT *
FROM employees
WHERE department = 'IT'
AND YEAR(joining_date) = 2022;
```

## Q26. Find employees who have completed more than 1000 days in the company.

```sql
SELECT emp_name, joining_date,
       DATEDIFF(CURDATE(), joining_date) AS days_in_company
FROM employees
WHERE DATEDIFF(CURDATE(), joining_date) > 1000;
```

## Q27. Display employee name, joining date and weekday name.

```sql
SELECT emp_name,
       joining_date,
       DAYNAME(joining_date) AS weekday
FROM employees;
```

## Q28. Display employee's birth month and joining month.

```sql
SELECT emp_name,
       MONTHNAME(birth_date) AS birth_month,
       MONTHNAME(joining_date) AS joining_month
FROM employees;
```

## Q29. Calculate the date when each employee completes 5 years in the company.

```sql
SELECT emp_name,
       joining_date,
       DATE_ADD(joining_date, INTERVAL 5 YEAR) AS five_year_completion
FROM employees;
```

## Q30. Find the longest-serving employee.

```sql
SELECT *
FROM employees
ORDER BY joining_date ASC
LIMIT 1;
```

